Enterprise Human Resources and IT Security Policy
Manual
Document Version: 2026.1 | Effective Date: January 1, 2026
1. Employee Leave and Attendance Policy
1.1 Annual Leave: All full-time employees accrue 24 days of paid annual leave per calendar year,
accrued at a rate of 2 days per month. Unused annual leave can be carried over up to a maximum of 10
days into the following year.
1.2 Sick Leave: Employees are entitled to 12 days of paid sick leave per year. Medical certificates are
required for consecutive absences exceeding 3 working days.
1.3 Maternity and Paternity Leave: Primary caregivers are entitled to 26 weeks of paid maternity leave.
Secondary caregivers are entitled to 4 weeks of paid paternity leave, which may be taken within the first
year of the child's birth or adoption.
1.4 Attendance Calculation: Attendance is calculated based on a standard 40-hour work week (8 hours
per day, Monday through Friday). Biometric or digital badge check-ins are mandatory. Attendance
falling below 90% in a quarter without approved leave results in an HR review.
2. Information Security and Remote Work Guidelines
2.1 Password Policy: All corporate accounts must use multi-factor authentication (MFA) and passwords
of at least 12 characters, mixing uppercase, lowercase, numbers, and symbols. Passwords must be
rotated every 90 days.
2.2 Remote Work & VPN: Remote work is permitted up to 2 days per week with manager approval.
When accessing internal company repositories or databases from outside the corporate network,
employees must connect via the official company VPN client.
2.3 Bring Your Own Device (BYOD): Personal devices used for work purposes must have corporate
Mobile Device Management (MDM) software installed and encrypted storage enabled.
2.4 Incident Reporting: Any suspected security breach, phishing email, or lost hardware must be
reported to the IT Security Team within 2 hours of discovery at security@enterprise.com.
3. Compensation, Benefits, and Performance Reviews
3.1 Salary & Bonuses: Salaries are disbursed on the last working day of each month. Annual
performance-based bonuses are awarded in March based on company and individual goal
achievement.
3.2 Health Insurance: Comprehensive health, dental, and vision insurance is provided for all full-time
employees and up to 3 dependents, fully subsidized by the company.
3.3 Performance Reviews: Formal performance reviews are conducted semi-annually in June and
December. Promotions and merit increments are determined during the December review cycle.
4. Code of Conduct and Grievance Redressal
4.1 Anti-Harassment: The company maintains a zero-tolerance policy towards discrimination and
harassment of any form. Violations will lead to immediate disciplinary action up to termination.
4.2 Whistleblower Protection: Employees can report ethical violations anonymously via the Ethics
Hotline. Retaliation against any whistleblower will result in severe legal and disciplinary action.
